Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_backup_header_restores_the_table_it_was_written_from`.

The defect: the backup header is written with the primary header's entry array location, so it points
at the array near the start of the disk instead of the copy just below itself. A disk whose primary
header is lost would be restored from a backup that names the wrong array.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that the backup's array lies after the last usable block,
on any disk large enough to hold the table: the array named is the primary's, at block 2.
diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs
index 0e923df03..05ff5f500 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs
@@ -509,7 +509,6 @@ impl<'a> PartitionTable<'a> {
         Header {
             my_logical_block_address: self.header.alternate_logical_block_address,
             alternate_logical_block_address: self.header.my_logical_block_address,
-            entry_array_logical_block_address: self.backup_entry_array_logical_block_address(),
             ..self.header
         }
     }
